A Frust app created with `frust create`.

## Theming

This app uses the **Glyph design system** by default — brought in as the
`frust-glyph` plugin crate dependency in `Cargo.toml` and installed by the
`frust_glyph::install()` call in `src/lib.rs`'s `frust::app!(setup = {..})`
block — which automatically adapts to the device's light/dark preference.
To swap to Material 3 or Cupertino instead, replace the `frust-glyph`
dependency with `frust-material`/`frust-cupertino` and swap the setup call:

```rust
frust::app!(MyAppApp, setup = {
    // Material 3 (M3)
    frust_material::install();

    // Or Cupertino
    // frust_cupertino::install();
});
```

Each `install()` is shorthand for
`frust::set_default_theme(frust_material::baseline())` /
`frust::set_default_theme(frust_cupertino::baseline())` — call
`set_default_theme` directly instead if you want the tokens without the
crate's install-timing contract.

## Custom Fonts

By default, this app's Glyph design system bundles IBM Plex Mono and Space
Mono fonts (`frust-glyph`'s `install()` registers them unconditionally — see
above). Dropping the `frust-glyph` dependency (or swapping to
`frust-material`/`frust-cupertino`, neither of which bundles a font) drops
the bundled fonts too.

Register your own fonts at app startup regardless of design system:

```rust
use frust::register_app_fonts;

fn init() {
    register_app_fonts(&[
        ("MyFont", include_bytes!("../assets/MyFont.ttf")),
    ]);
}
```

## Theme Customization

Customize colors, motion, and spacing using the builder:

```rust
use frust::{ColorScheme, Theme};

let custom = Theme::builder()
    .light_scheme(ColorScheme {
        // ... customize roles
    })
    .build();
set_app_theme(custom);
```

See `frust-theme`'s docs in the Frust repo for the full token reference.
